  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency drought response to Pastoral and Agro-pastoral households in Baydhaba and Burhakaba districts of Bay region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $5m FAO project is to enable household to immediately cover their basic needs and to contribute to the rehabilitation of productive community assets. To that end, FAO will distribute about $3.7m in cash to 53,286 people for a duration of 4-5 months and pay 8,946 people for repair of assets like water catchments, water canals, livestock water points, etc. In total, the project will target 62,232 people, including 16,740 women and 13,753 girls.</narrative>
  </description>
